mips: declare local assembly symbols before use

Clang's integrated assembler expands PIC `la` macros as soon as they are
parsed. When a local symbol is defined later in the file, LLVM does not yet
know its binding and emits a lone R_MIPS_GOT16 (without the required
R_MIPS_LO16 pair). Under the MIPS ELF ABI the linker then stores the 64 KiB
page address in the GOT while the generated code expects a full address,
corrupting the SHA-256 K-table and AES T-table pointers.

Declare the internal AES functions and the AES/SHA tables local before any
reference to work around this assembler limitation.

Adapted from OpenSSL PR #32620 for openssl-3.1.5-quic1.
Link: https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/issues/65020
Link: https://github.com/openssl/openssl/pull/32620
---
--- a/crypto/aes/asm/aes-mips.pl
+++ b/crypto/aes/asm/aes-mips.pl
@@ -110,6 +110,12 @@
 #include "mips_arch.h"
 
 .text
+.local	_mips_AES_encrypt
+.local	_mips_AES_decrypt
+.local	_mips_AES_set_encrypt_key
+.local	AES_Te
+.local	AES_Td
+.local	AES_Te4
 #if !defined(__mips_eabi) && (!defined(__vxworks) || defined(__pic__))
 .option	pic2
 #endif
--- a/crypto/sha/asm/sha512-mips.pl
+++ b/crypto/sha/asm/sha512-mips.pl
@@ -311,6 +311,7 @@
 #include "mips_arch.h"
 
 .text
+.local	K${label}
 .set	noat
 #if !defined(__mips_eabi) && (!defined(__vxworks) || defined(__pic__))
 .option	pic2
